Write the field in terms of a scalar potential $\phi$. In the sign convention used on the board, $\mathbf E=\nabla\phi,
  \qquad
  \nabla\cdot\mathbf E=\rho,$ and therefore $\nabla^2\phi
  =\frac{\partial^2\phi}{\partial x^2}
  +\frac{\partial^2\phi}{\partial y^2}
  =\rho.$ In a charge-free region this reduces to Laplace’s equation, $\nabla^2\phi=0.$

